      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let R represent the event that it will rain on a given day. Let $P(R)$ be the probability it rain on a particular day.\n\nIf the probability it will rain on Saturday is $60\\%$, then $P(R) = 0.60$.\n\nIf the probability it will rain on Sunday is $25\\%$, then $P(R) = 0.25$.\n\nBecause the probability of rain on a given day is independent of the weather on any other day,\n$P(R \\cap \\text{sun}) = P(R) \\cdot P(R)$\n$= (0.60)(0.25)$\n$= \\boxed{0.15} \\text{ or } 15\\%$ **Therefore, the probability it will rain on both days is equal to $\\boxed{15\\%}$.**",
